  "raw_label": "1",
  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Thippugaari Venkateswara Reddy vs The State Of Andhra Pradesh on 16 October, 2019 Author: U. Durga Prasad Rao Bench: U. Durga Prasad Rao Hon'Ble Sri Justice U. Durga Prasad Rao Criminal Petition No.6136 Of 2019 Order:",
    "facts": "The petitionerd/A1 and A2 seek to quash the proceedings against them in Crime No.88 of 2018 of Koilakuntla Police Station, Kurnool District, which was registered against them for the offences under Sections 188, 273 of IPC and Secs.26, 30 of Food Safety and Standards Act, 2006 (for short 'FSS Act, 2006). 2. The allegations against the petitioners briefly are that on 26.10.2018 at about 03:45 P.M., the complainant along with his staff on credible information proceeded to the Pan shop of A1 situated besides SBI ATM, State Bank Road, Koilakuntla, Kurnool District, where A1 tried to run away towards the market, on questioning, he revealed that he purchased the banned tobacco products from A2. Later, the complainant seized the said banned tobacco products under a cover of panchanama, arrested the accused and he registered the same as a case in Crime No.88 of 2018 for the offences stated supra.",
    "arguments": "3. Learned counsel for petitioners while denying the FIR allegations would submit that even if the prosecution case is accepted to be true, tobacco products would not fall within the definition of Section 3(j) of FSS Act and therefore, the Police are not authorized to register the crime, investigate and file charge sheet and therefore, registration of the FIR is contrary to the provisions of FSS Act.",
    "petitioner_arguments": "3. Learned counsel for petitioners while denying the FIR allegations would submit that even if the prosecution case is accepted to be true, tobacco products would not fall within the definition of Section 3(j) of FSS Act and therefore, the Police are not authorized to register the crime, investigate and file charge sheet and therefore, registration of the FIR is contrary to the provisions of FSS Act.",
